  "solution": "Given:\n\n(4, 1024, 64)\n\n(225, 81, 135)\n\n**Logic:** [ (a)², (b)², (a × b)]\n\n**(4, 1024, 64) →**\n\n⇒ [(2)², (32)², (32 × 2)]\n\n⇒ [(4), (1024), (64)]\n\n**(225, 81, 135) →**\n\n⇒ [(15)2, (9)2, (15 × 9)]\n\n⇒ [(225), (81), (135)]\n\nChecking all the given options:\n\n**1. **(30, 676, 78)\n\n⇒ [(5 × 6), (26)², (26 × 3)]\n\n**2.** (27, 125, 15)\n\n⇒ [(3)³, (5)³, (3 × 5)]\n\n⇒ [ (27), (125), (15)]\n\n**3. (49, 841, 203)**\n\n⇒ [(7)2, (29)2, (7 × 29)]\n\n⇒ [(49), (841), (203)]\n\n**4.** (64, 256, 512)\n\n⇒ [(8)2, (16)2, (8 × 16)]\n\n⇒ [(64), (256), (128)]\n\nHere,** (49, 841, 203) **shows a similar relation to the given set of numbers.\n\nHence, the correct answer is \"Option (3)\".",
